# Keep the plan in step with the code

The user asked (2026-10-01): "For everything we update, remember to also update the plan."

After any change to the site's behaviour, look or content:

- Update the current milestone plan in `docs/plan/` (split by area on
  2026-10-02; `docs/plan/README.md` says which file holds what):
  - the area file for that feature, describing how the site is now;
  - one dated entry in `docs/plan/CHANGELOG.md` (what, why, files);
  - `docs/plan/checks.md` only if an acceptance check or budget figure changes.
- Mark user-requested changes with "(user request, YYYY-MM-DD)" or
  "(user choice, YYYY-MM-DD)".
- New or changed artwork, textures or fonts also go in `docs/ASSET-LEDGER.md`
  with source and rights.
- Commit the plan edits together with the code change.

Do not edit the planning files in `~/.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`; the user keeps
those unchanged.

